# Gravwell Office 365 Kit
****

This kit is designed to provide an out-of-the-box experience for working with Office 365 logs.

An integration guide is available on [this documentation page](https://docs.gravwell.io/integrations/cloud/office365.html)

This kit provides the following utilities:

- Queries
    - Detections
    - Stats
- Dashboards
- Scheduled Searches
- Actionables
- Macros
- Templates

Refer to the Kit Overview playbook for more detail on these components.

## Dependencies
- Gravwell Network Enrichment Kit

## Changelog:
****

**v5: Audit remediation**

- Adds: Kit Overview and Copy of Readme playbooks
- Fixes: 365-exchange autoextractor (shipped as a byte-for-byte copy of 365-azure — wrong tag/fields, missing MANIFEST entry)
- Fixes: SharePoint tag macro name mismatch (declared O365-SHAREPOINT, referenced everywhere as 365-SHAREPOINT — SharePoint queries silently unconfigurable)
- Fixes: Azure Active Users numbercard (filtered on "Success"; the Management Activity API emits "Succeeded")
- Fixes: login-failure table (dropped UserType before the lookup meant to display it)
- Fixes: attachment-extension donut (case-folded after grouping, producing duplicate slices)
- Fixes: General ThreatIntel chart (filtered a RecordType name as if it were a Workload value)
- Fixes: Exchange IP template (grouped on LogonError, a field that only exists on Azure AD events)
- Fixes: login-ratio calculation (divided by a zero success count, producing +Inf/NaN for exactly the password-spray rows the table exists to rank)
- Fixes: two duplicate MANIFEST declarations and a searchlibrary copy of the scheduled login-history search (running the copy by hand overwrote the scheduled job's resource)
- Fixes: dashboard search aliases and an Azure-labelled pivot that actually targeted an Exchange template
- Changes: renamed "ThreatManagement Alerts" to "Security & Compliance Alerts" and "Active Users" to "Active Mail Users" to match what each actually measures
- Changes: replaced inlined lookup stages with the RESOLVE\_O365\_RECORDTYPE/RESOLVE\_O365\_USERTYPE macros the kit already shipped
- Changes: pruned three dead search entries, removed authoring-instance searchID residue, added workload labels to every searchlibrary item, filled in empty names/descriptions
- Changes: replaced the stub MANIFEST.Readme with this document
- Changes: kit branding images (icon, banner, cover) replaced with standard Gravwell art
